   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Just as color is controlled with the colour aesthetic, line type and\r<br>thickness are controlled by the size and linetype aesthetics.  See\r<br><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_density.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_density.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383308266000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Qck0FkdvELk42wPrj8BLm\">http://had.co.nz/ggplot2/geom_density.html</a>  These can either be set to\r<br>a single value outside the aes call, or mapped to a variable inside\r<br>it.\r<br>\r<br>If  you need more help than this, a reproducible example would be\r<br>necessary to show what you have done and are trying to do\r<br>\r<br>--Brian Diggs\r<br>\r<br>On May 16, 9:35 am, &quot;Zodet, Marc W. (AHRQ)&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Marc.Zo...@ahrq.hhs.gov</a>&gt;\r<br>wrote:\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; Hello all,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve just begun using ggplot2.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I can&#39;t find a way to change a few of the line characteristics for some\r<br>&gt; (overlaid) density plots I&#39;ve generated.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve been able to change the colors used, but not types and thickness of\r<br>&gt; the lines.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Any guidance would be much appreciated.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thanks in advance.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Marc\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Marc W. Zodet, MS\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Senior Health Statistician\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Center for Financing, Access, and Cost Trends\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"tel:(301)%20427-1563\" value=\"+13014271563\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">301-427-1563</a> (Tel)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"tel:(301)%20427-1276\" value=\"+13014271276\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">301-427-1276</a> (Fax)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
